#, no-wrap
msgid "Chaos army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$chaos.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:76
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/goblins.adoc:95
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[trolls,†2]]2. Trolls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:86
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:97
msgid ""
"When trying to issue an order to a unit of Trolls or to a brigade that "
"contains a unit of Trolls, any Command penalty applied for distance between "
"the character and the Troll unit is always doubled. So at 20cm no penalty "
"applies, at 40cm −2, at 60cm −4, and so on. Trolls can regenerate wounds – "
"in each round of combat after whole stands have been removed Trolls "
"automatically regenerate one outstanding hit. If no hits are left over after "
"removing whole stands then regeneration has no effect. Regenerated hits "
"still count towards the combat result for the round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[harpies,†3]]3. Harpies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:91
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Harpies are based facing the long edge of the base in the same way as "
"infantry, rather than the short edge like other monsters. Harpies can fly. A "
"unit of harpies cannot be joined by a character."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[spawn,†5]]5. Spawn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Spawn units have −1 Command penalty if not part of a brigade that includes "
"more non-Spawn units than Spawn units. Up to two Spawn units can be included "
"in any brigade and do not count towards the maximum size of that brigade."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[chaos-dragon,†6]]6. Chaos Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:114
msgid "Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride a Chaos Dragon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:115
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[chariot-mount,†7]]7. Chariot Mount"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Generals, Sorcerers and Heroes can ride Chariots. An extra +1 Attack is "
"added to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chaos spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boon of Chaos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:128
msgid ""
"_A dark power billows from the Sorcerer filling his troops with the "
"destructive vigour of chaos._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:132
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast if the Sorcerer has joined a unit in combat.  The "
"spell affects the unit he has joined. The effect lasts for the duration of "
"the following Combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:138
msgid ""
"Every stand in the unit, including characters that have joined the unit, "
"adds +1 to its Attacks value. As the Sorcerer must join the unit to cast the "
"spell this includes the Sorcerer himself, but it is possible for other "
"characters to join the unit as well, in which case the +1 is applied to "
"whichever character fights."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anger of the Gods"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:145
msgid ""
"_The anger of the chaos gods blots out the sun and sends clouds of rage "
"scudding across the battlefield all around the Sorcerer._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:148
msgid ""
"The spell is cast upon the Sorcerer himself and affects all enemy units "
"within 30cm of the stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:151
msgid "The spell lasts until the end of the opposing player’s following turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:157
msgid ""
"The spell affects the opposing army’s ability to issue commands.  All enemy "
"units within 30cm of the Chaos Sorcerer suffer a −1 Command penalty. This "
"penalty is applied when each order is issued: a unit might therefore be "
"within 30cm of the Sorcerer for one order but not for a second, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rage of Chaos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:165
msgid ""
"_The Sorcerer screams a blasphemous litany to his dark gods.  From the black "
"gore that drenches the battlefield leaps a roaring daemonic shadow that "
"fights with great madness and ferocity._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:169
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a friendly unit that is engaged in combat and "
"which is within range. The Sorcerer does not have to be able to see the "
"target to cast the spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:173
msgid ""
"The affect lasts for the duration of the following combat phase and the "
"indicated bonus attacks are added to the unit’s total attacks each round."
msgstr ""

#.  – changed to ,
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:186
msgid ""
"The unit gains bonus Rage of Chaos attacks for the following combat phase. "
"To determine the number of bonus attacks roll one D6 at a time and add the "
"results together. The player can roll as many D6 as he wishes up to a "
"maximum of 1 per stand in the unit. The player always rolls one dice at a "
"time and can decide to stop at any point. However, if the player rolls a "
"second or subsequent dice and scores the same value as any previously rolled "
"dice, then the total Rage of Chaos attacks are directed against the targeted "
"unit instead of its enemy. Rage of Chaos attacks that rebound in this way "
"are struck only once in the first round of combat: they are not struck each "
"round."
msgstr ""

#.  Spacing around + fixed.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:190
msgid ""
"Example, 1 + 4 + 6 = 11 extra attacks for the Chaos unit each round. 1 + 4 + "
"1 = 6 Attacks upon the Chaos unit in the first round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "Curse of Chaos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:200
msgid ""
"An arc of pure energy strikes the foe, wreaking monstrous changes, melting "
"flesh and twisting bones into monstrous form.  This spell can be cast on an "
"enemy unit. The Sorcerer must be able to see his target to use this spell. "
"The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged in combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:205
msgid ""
"The Curse of Chaos is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks except "
"that armour has no effect (all targets count as having no armour). A unit "
"can be driven back by a Curse of Chaos as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""
